#: ../../source/reference/design/parallelism.md:1
msgid "Parallelism as a consequence"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/design/parallelism.md:3
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"*Implemented.* Nothing in {doc}`pages`, {doc}`classification`, "
"{doc}`schedule` or {doc}`segments` mentions threads. That is the point: "
"parallelism was **added without redesigning anything**, because the page "
"had been the unit of work all along."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/design/parallelism.md:7
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"This page is why the levels are what they are. How to drive them is "
"{doc}`../../guides/user/advanced/parallelism`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/design/parallelism.md:9
msgid "What the profiler found in four real reports"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/design/parallelism.md:10
msgid ""
"Four real reports, 29 to 1,824 pages, profiled through the spans the "
"engine already carries:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/design/parallelism.md
msgid "Finding"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/design/parallelism.md
msgid "Measure"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/design/parallelism.md
msgid "loading the PDF through PyMuPDF"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/design/parallelism.md
msgid "**35–75%** of a job"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/design/parallelism.md
msgid "page classification"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/design/parallelism.md
msgid "between 1:8.5 and 1:157 of the extraction steps"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/design/parallelism.md
msgid "`text_filter`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/design/parallelism.md
#, python-format
msgid "85–96% of the engine's own work"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/design/parallelism.md
msgid "one pipe inside it — the standard investments text filter, pure Rust"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/design/parallelism.md
msgid "**30–54%** of a whole job"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/design/parallelism.md
msgid "`deserialize`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/design/parallelism.md
msgid "under **0.2%** everywhere"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/design/parallelism.md:20
msgid "Two of those numbers changed the plan, and one of them reversed it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/design/parallelism.md:22
msgid "Jobs get processes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/design/parallelism.md:24
msgid ""
"Because the dominant cost is **behind the GIL**. PyMuPDF is Python; "
"threads would have re-serialised precisely the part worth parallelising."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/design/parallelism.md:27
msgid ""
"The children send their results back over IPC and the **parent writes the"
" output once**, so the observable behaviour does not change."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/design/parallelism.md:30
msgid ""
"**Rejected: letting each child write its own output.** It is simpler and "
"it would have changed what batch mode produces — ten directories instead "
"of one set of tables with a `Report` column. A parallelism strategy that "
"changes the product is not a parallelism strategy."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/design/parallelism.md:34
msgid "Pages get threads"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/design/parallelism.md:36
msgid ""
"Inside a job, the pages of a step run on a thread pool **the crate "
"owns**, not rayon's global one."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/design/parallelism.md:38
msgid ""
"A library must not seize the thread pool of the program embedding it. "
"This one is a Python extension module as well as a binary, so \"the "
"embedding program\" is a real thing with its own plans."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/design/parallelism.md:41
msgid ""
"Pipes **declare whether they scale with threads**, defaulting to yes, and"
" the three Python pipe kinds declare no. A format whose work is an "
"author's Python pipe therefore runs sequentially rather than contending "
"for the GIL — measured, 182 ms → 189 ms between one thread and twenty, "
"against 7.2 s → 1.0 s for an entirely structured format on the same "
"machine."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/design/parallelism.md:46
msgid "Two planned levels were cancelled by the measurements"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/design/parallelism.md:48
msgid ""
"This is the part worth reading twice, because it is the opposite of what "
"a plan usually produces."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/design/parallelism.md:50
msgid ""
"**Page classes and pipelines within a step** — cancelled. It would sit on"
" top of a loop that already saturates the machine: two nested units of "
"work in rayon with no free threads to give them. The pathological case it"
" was meant to serve — very few pages, many heavy pipelines — **does not "
"exist in the corpus**: the smallest of 21 real reports has 29 pages, more"
" than the machine has threads."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/design/parallelism.md:55
#, python-format
msgid ""
"**Deserialization blocks above a threshold** — cancelled. It would have "
"addressed 0.2% of runtime."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/design/parallelism.md:57
msgid ""
"Both were **removed from the design** rather than shipped as options that"
" default to off. An option that is off by default never runs, is "
"therefore never exercised, and still has to be maintained at every change"
" to the code it wraps. A feature that exists only to honour an earlier "
"plan is a maintenance cost with no user."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/design/parallelism.md:62
msgid "What parallelism costs in memory"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/design/parallelism.md
msgid "gain"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/design/parallelism.md
msgid ""
"39.4 s → 16.7 s (**2.36×**) on two large reports, defaults, output byte-"
"identical"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/design/parallelism.md
msgid "price"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/design/parallelism.md
msgid "peak memory 783 MB → **~1.2 GB**, growing with concurrent jobs"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/design/parallelism.md:68
msgid ""
"The memory is the real price, and it is why the job level is the one "
"worth turning down on a small machine: `--jobs 1` keeps page-level "
"threading and drops the concurrent copies of the document, giving up the "
"smaller of the two gains."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/design/parallelism.md:72
msgid "An optimisation not taken: the hottest pipe"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/design/parallelism.md:73
#, python-format
msgid ""
"The single hottest pipe — 30–54% of a job, pure Rust, single-threaded and"
" deterministic — has never been optimised internally. Indexing the target"
" companies instead of scanning them, and reducing regex compilation per "
"call, could plausibly be worth as much as the whole parallelism effort, "
"with **no** risk to determinism."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/design/parallelism.md:78
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"It is recorded here rather than done, because it is a separate piece of "
"work with its own measurements to take. {doc}`limits`."
msgstr ""

